eally really cool Bhutanese building  that I think a lot of people will  recognize or if you haven't seen it  before you definitely should check it  out it's called the Tiger's Nest well I  don't think officially so but it's a  monastery on the cliff side of a  mountain and it's absolutely beautiful  it's really cool there are probably some  pictures of it on reddit that go viral  every month or so but yeah it's really  cool to see just how it's integrated  into the natural environments and how  you see all of these ideas coming back  in this building it's just generally a  building then I recommend looking up and  just falling over how cool it looks now  at this point the observation building  is finished so I went ahead and put in  the rest of the actual habitats and  started working on the rook work and  foliage and things like that you might  notice then I didn't record everything I  did I did cut some parts out of this  time that stores a lot of just moving  around and tinkering about with certain  things I added the rock wall at the back  the habitats here which looks much nicer  I think than just a wooden fence I did  add a wooden fence here and there  because realistically I don't think as  you would be able to afford a rock wall  around an entire habitat as large as  this one but wherever I could and  especially where it was very much in  view I wanted to make the barrier a rock  work facade as well to try and make  everything look a bit more realistic and  immersive and I'm just tailing the paths  here a little bit although I have to say  I'm really not focusing on the paths  that much I'll be keeping those mostly  as they are I think if I had more time  or if this habitat was smaller I would  have really just detailed everything and  did everything myself but can be really  time-consuming to do that and we only  have so much time in the beta know this  is still a beta in the end so I wanted  to keep that for another day maybe in  some future zoos our experiments more  with that for now I really wanted to  keep the the focus for the rest of the  video on trying to build the habitat  itself and trying to make it look as  natural as possible while also keeping  the Tigers inside the habitat and  keeping all of the humans outside the  habitat preferably as well  although I'm very glad we don't have to  worry about little kids jumping into  habitats as far as I'm aware I do want  to make it look safe enough just for  realism purposes so there's that as well  oh and at this point I suppose I did  start to detail the building a little  bit more because it was looking a little  bit empty and undecorated and I found  some inspiration just from hanging a  bunch of different fabrics outside give  it some color some more detail it's bit  over the top and a bit kitschy I think  but at the same time I think it just  makes it look much more inviting and  charming so I just went ahead and ended  that stuff in there Bhutan isn't quite  India of course but it's close so I  think some of the Indian scenery pieces  can definitely help at least giving the  idea of  boutonnieres detailing and on the inside  I put a bunch of props I'm not the  biggest fan of props in zoos but given  that this building is trying to pretend  being a traditional building and trying  to set the setting of an actual  Bhutanese area I think it's fitting to  at least add some props and make it feel  a tiny bit lived in to just help with  the general immersiveness of the area  and that is basically it for all that at  this point I started working on another  shelter I do already have one shelter  made out of rocks on the other side of  the habitat so that should be fine but I  didn't want to have one main shelter  next to the gates where employees will  get in and deliver the food and all that  so I'm building a very simple shelter  here very generally inspired by the roof  shape of Bhutanese buildings but it's  not really specifically based on  anything this is all quite simple and it  won't be that visible from a guests  perspective there will definitely be  some trees and things like that to hide  the view a little bit but this will be  the main and the largest shelter for the  Tigers I was also considering building  an actual indoor section where Tigers  can go to I haven't worked on that in  this video and I think it shouldn't be  too much of an issue given that the  climates of this region is at least  acceptable for the Tigers but if I ever  decide to add some sort of indoor  section where guests can look at the  Tigers indoors I can always attach it to  this building or on the other side of  the habitats I don't know it's it's a  possibility but in this case I didn't go  quite all the way there and honestly I  was happy with how the habitats is so  far anyway so yeah there's that also I  added a waterfall here which you didn't  see me do on video because I cut that  section out as well but I needed to add  that I noticed that pretty much every  youtuber who is ending a waterfall in an  enclosure so I was like who am i if I  don't add a waterfall to this enclosure  so decided to get that element out there  you know you need to do it at some point  anyway so might as well do it  but now honestly I thought it looks  really good in this position and I  thought it would also look nice from a  gas perspective if you're looking from  the house of course I'm trying to still  keep in mind the different sight lines  that guests will see when they're  looking into the habitat so that was  definitely part of that decision as well  and finally I'm adding some important  buildings in the back here but yeah that  is basically it for this build so I'm  gonna leave you guys with some clips of  habitat and you can see the Tigers  enjoying it here I only have two Tigers  so not too much the film but as far as  I've been able to tell I've tested them  for quite a while they are not able to  escape thankfully and scare off any  guests so that is nice  they've been enjoying the outside and  really running around quite a lot and  they seem to be fine in fact even the  terrain coverage and the foliage was  perfectly fine I didn't even have to  fine-tune that which was a total luck  because I really wasn't sure if this  terrain was gonna be suitable but yeah  I'm very glad that it is I didn't really  have to think ER with anything anymore  after putting the Tigers in I just added  some habitat things enrichment items and  things like that of course so yeah I'm  very happy with this habitat and I hope  you guys liked watching me build it and  if I have enough time between my  university obligations which I will  actually attend to to some degree I  would like to build some other habitats  but regardless I'll try and do some  other stuff in the planet to beta as  well so keep your eyes out for some  future videos anyway that's been it  thank you guys for watching and I hope  to see you next time  [Music]  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

